 "result": "Body: squeeze.py, a stdlib-only wrapper that compresses stdin with LZMA2 raw format at preset 9e (dict 8 MiB) in mode c and decompresses in mode d. It passes the round-trip check on the public samples in-0.txt and in-1.txt, and the assay registered a baseline of 5.47469. The two tuned variants (lc=4/pb=0/lp=0 with nice_len 273, and a 16 MiB dictionary with depth 1000) scored 5.498 and 5.493, about +0.4%, which is below the 3% win threshold, so the incumbent was kept. I am resting because further LZMA parameter tweaks are unlikely to clear the threshold, and a context-mixing coder in pure Python would probably exceed the 30 s limit on ~700 KB inputs.",
